      "source": [
        "##Single linear neuron/perceptron without activation and hidden layer\n",
        "\n",
        "Input (x) -> Linear neuron: y = w*x  -> Output (y_pred)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Y-84tcepgKgW"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "YL0FU3Hjf_5I"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import random\n",
        "\n",
        "x=2\n",
        "label=17\n",
        "l_r=0.1 #learning rate for not overshoot or very slow progress\n",
        "w=random.uniform(-1.0, 1.0) #random weight\n",
        "\n",
        "for i in range(1000):\n",
        "    #multiply weight with input\n",
        "    y_pred=w*x\n",
        "\n",
        "    #compute the loss\n",
        "    loss=(y_pred-label)**2\n",
        "\n",
        "    #backpropagation (applying power rule for each to form a chain rule)\n",
        "    #find dl(loss)/dw(weight), so need to find:\n",
        "    #dl/dy_pred*dy/dy_pred\n",
        "    #general chain rule formula is:\n",
        "    #dl/dw=dl/(dy_pred)*(dy_pred/dw)\n",
        "    #result is below\n",
        "    slope = 2 * (y_pred - label) * x\n",
        "\n",
        "    #gradient descent\n",
        "    #this update new weight(that optmize to get closer to 'label' value)\n",
        "    #the updated weight should be closer or get to label value over time\n",
        "    #adjust the learning parameter to experiment on how long or fast to converge on more complex input and weight\n",
        "    w=w-l_r*slope\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(w)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "to check what true weight for satisfying the label value, calculate below:\n",
        "-we first find rate of change of loss w.r.t weight where the value of slope is 0, means the optimal one for weight in order for equal to the value of target/label, when this weight multiplied with x(input).\n",
        "\n",
        "dL/dw​=2(w×x−y)×x=0\n",
        "\n",
        "then, divide both side by 2, and use zero product property(A*B=0, so A=0 and B=0):\n",
        "\n",
        "case 1: 2(w×x−y)=0\n",
        "case 2: x=0\n",
        "\n",
        "solve:\n",
        "\n",
        "c1:w = y/x\n",
        "and for c2, its depending on the value of x itself on beginning, if it is 0, then it will always become true(which is 0) regardless of any weight value\n",
        "\n",
        "-in this case the x is 2, so plug in to y/x:\n",
        "w=y/x (which is the value of weight needed to get optimum target)\n",
        "\n"
      ],
